[info] ========== CONCEPTS ==========
[info] Pair RDD: Booking events are converted into key-value pairs using hotel ID as the key.
[info] Window Operations: A 10-second window with a 5-second sliding interval is used to detect booking activity.
[info] Broadcast: Small hotel reference data is broadcast to Spark executors to avoid repeatedly sending the same data.
[info] State: Booking and cancellation changes are maintained using a running occupancy state for each hotel.
[info] Occupancy: Current occupied rooms are calculated from previous occupancy plus booking or cancellation changes.
[info] Spark SQL: Booking events are converted into a DataFrame and queried using SQL for reporting.
[info] Partitioning: Booking RDDs use multiple partitions so Spark can process data in parallel.
[info] Streaming: Spark Streaming processes booking events as micro-batches.
